{% comment %}
  The home page body: a list of pieces, the newest first. Kept out of
  _pages/home.md so it stays indented — prettier flattens HTML nested in the
  Markdown page. Wrapped in one element so kramdown passes it through untouched.
  Each piece is something to play with, then a line on where it leads.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="home">
  <p class="pieces-intro">Mertcan Özdemir · MRI, ice hockey, small electronics</p>

  <div class="pieces">
    <section class="piece is-lead" aria-labelledby="piece-kspace" data-kspace>
      <div class="piece-art kspace">
        <figure>
          <canvas data-k aria-label="k-space: move over it to measure more lines"></canvas>
          <figcaption>k-space</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <canvas data-img role="img" aria-label="The image rebuilt from the measured lines"></canvas>
          <figcaption>image</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <div class="piece-text">
        <h2 class="piece-title" id="piece-kspace">Why does an MRI take so long?</h2>
        <p class="piece-desc">
          A scanner does not take a picture. It measures k‑space, the image's frequencies, one line at a time. Here only every fourth line was
          measured: the scan took a quarter of the time, and the head folds over itself. Move over k‑space to measure the rest.
        </p>
        <p class="kspace-status">
          <span data-status aria-live="polite"></span>
          <button type="button" data-reset>start again</button>
        </p>
        <a class="piece-more" href="https://icon-lab.github.io/mri-recon-comparison-graph/"
          >How the methods that fill in the missing lines compare&nbsp;→</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>

    <a class="piece is-lead is-flip" href="{{ '/drills/' | relative_url }}">
      <span class="piece-art piece-drill" data-drill="two-on-one-give-and-go" data-preview>
        <svg viewBox="-30.6 -16.8 61.2 34.2" aria-hidden="true">
          <g class="trails"></g>
          <g class="events"></g>
          <g class="actors"></g>
        </svg>
      </span>
      <span class="piece-text">
        <span class="piece-title">Hockey drills, animated</span>
        <span class="piece-desc">Fifty-two practice drills you can play step by step.</span>
        <span class="piece-more">See the drills&nbsp;→</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </div>
</div>
